From 75b042a3b966ea87588419bf38e27f437b7718e1 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Andrey Stoyan <andrey.stoyan.csam@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 15 Aug 2026 18:29:20 +0300
Subject: [PATCH 16/44] fix(chexc): assumption-import changes invalidate the
 incremental cache (E3)

'HashImportSpec' hashed the import's kind, paths, identifier and alias but not
its annotations, so editing an '@AssumeThrows' list changed no hash: the
declarations kept their obligations from the previous build and were never
re-checked. A file whose assumed list shrank kept compiling as though the old
assumptions still held.

Import-spec changes roll the package back to a full compilation
(IncrementalScopeAnalysis.cpp: "package or import specs changed"), so hashing
the annotations there inherits exactly that granularity -- coarse, but
over-approximate in the safe direction and independent of how proposal 5.2.2's
per-file vs per-package scoping is eventually ruled (author-questions Q1).

Test-validity note, because the first attempt got this wrong: incr_assume's
two versions must differ ONLY in the annotation token. The first draft added
explanatory comments to the .new file, which shifted every declaration's
position, re-checked the file for unrelated reasons, and PASSED against the
unfixed compiler -- a false negative that would have retired a real ledger
entry. The .cached decision log exposed it ('run' and 'main' both marked
changed, when a pure annotation edit should mark nothing). The corrected pair
differs on line 1 alone and is red against the unfixed compiler: zero
diagnostics, nothing spread.

Tests: CheckedExceptions + IncrementalCompilation 2027/2027; ctest 49/49.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 src/Parse/ASTHasher.cpp | 11 +++++++++++
 1 file changed, 11 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/Parse/ASTHasher.cpp b/src/Parse/ASTHasher.cpp
index 7ac637b5..aa9a8bb7 100644
--- a/src/Parse/ASTHasher.cpp
+++ b/src/Parse/ASTHasher.cpp
@@ -380,6 +380,17 @@ struct ASTHasherImpl {
             }
         }
         SUPERHash<whatTypeToHash>(im.hasDoubleColon);
+        // Checked exceptions (proposal 5.2.2, ledger E3): an '@AssumeThrows' annotation imposes
+        // obligations on every call into the imported package, so changing its list changes what
+        // the file's declarations must supply -- exactly like changing the import itself. Without
+        // this the declarations keep their hashes and an incremental build never re-checks them,
+        // leaving the stale obligations in place. Import-spec changes roll the package back to a
+        // full compilation, which is coarse but the granularity this hash already has.
+        for (auto& anno : is.annotations) {
+            if (anno && anno->assumeThrows) {
+                SUPERHash<whatTypeToHash>(anno->assumeThrows);
+            }
+        }
     }
     template <int whatTypeToHash> void HashPackageSpec(const PackageSpec& ps)
     {
